1
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:02,748
Every child in our village

2
00:00:02,768 --> 00:00:04,033
knew the rule.

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:05,997
Never...

4
00:00:06,124 --> 00:00:07,622
leave the path.

5
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:11,534
The winter I turned seven,

6
00:00:11,554 --> 00:00:12,602
my mother tied a red

7
00:00:12,622 --> 00:00:13,693
hood under my chin,

8
00:00:13,713 --> 00:00:14,831
and gave me a basket

9
00:00:14,851 --> 00:00:16,256
for my grandmother.

10
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:17,773
I didn't

11
00:00:17,793 --> 00:00:19,256
have a grandmother.

12
00:00:19,465 --> 00:00:21,357
I didn't know that yet.

13
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:31,270
The path went down

14
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:32,489
into the valley.

15
00:00:32,509 --> 00:00:34,137
The deeper it went,

16
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:34,834
the quieter

17
00:00:34,854 --> 00:00:36,503
the world became.

18
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:40,763
Then the wolf came.

19
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:43,227
And everybody knows what

20
00:00:43,247 --> 00:00:45,476
wolves do to little girls.

21
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,821
It chased me off the path,

22
00:00:54,841 --> 00:00:56,223
up the ridge,

23
00:00:56,292 --> 00:00:58,092
into the deep snow.

24
00:00:58,405 --> 00:01:00,205
And then it stopped...

25
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:01,842
and waited.

26
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:07,763
From up there,

27
00:01:07,783 --> 00:01:08,436
I could see where

28
00:01:08,456 --> 00:01:09,919
the path ended.

29
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:11,743
There was a house.

30
00:01:11,763 --> 00:01:13,493
There was no grandmother.

31
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,634
Only red hoods.

32
00:01:15,654 --> 00:01:17,488
One for every winter.

33
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:22,675
The village called

34
00:01:22,695 --> 00:01:23,720
it Grandmother.

35
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:24,289
They fed it

36
00:01:24,309 --> 00:01:25,357
one child a year,

37
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:25,984
so it would leave

38
00:01:26,004 --> 00:01:27,617
the rest of them alone.

39
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:37,826
My mother had packed

40
00:01:37,846 --> 00:01:40,345
my basket herself. Bread.

41
00:01:40,365 --> 00:01:41,538
Wine.

42
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,496
And a lantern.

43
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:45,676
She couldn't save me.

44
00:01:45,696 --> 00:01:46,233
But she could

45
00:01:46,253 --> 00:01:47,600
give me fire.

46
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:54,162
Every winter,

47
00:01:54,182 --> 00:01:55,137
the wolf chased

48
00:01:55,157 --> 00:01:57,201
a child off the path.

49
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:58,704
And every winter,

50
00:01:58,724 --> 00:02:00,744
the child ran back.

51
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:02,051
Because we'd all

52
00:02:02,071 --> 00:02:03,131
been taught...

53
00:02:03,151 --> 00:02:04,788
never leave the path.

54
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,604
When I walked home,

55
00:02:07,624 --> 00:02:09,273
nobody cheered.

56
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,263
They looked at me

57
00:02:11,472 --> 00:02:13,330
like I was the monster.

58
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,546
They told every child

59
00:02:21,566 --> 00:02:22,196
she was walking

60
00:02:22,216 --> 00:02:24,051
to her grandmother's house.

61
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,786
So I became one.

62
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,434
Which path were you

63
00:02:30,454 --> 00:02:32,254
told never to leave?

